      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, with a fine day forecast though strong southwest winds from yesterday have eased only slightly and are still likely to affect lift operations. Groomers have been busy working in all the fresh snow, feeling like mid-winter with cold, dry cover; there's been 27 cm over the past 7 days, holding the natural base at 112 cm. It's currently 1°C with winds around 24 km/h gusting to 45 km/h. Coverage is excellent overall, though some areas have been stripped back by wind, with variable off-piste conditions including big drifts and wind-stripped sections. Main Basin and Valley View are running from 8:30am, with the T-Bar and Captains following; Soho started the day on wind hold before opening at 12:15pm, and McDougall's is running with chairs only after reopening at 11:45am; Willows is closed for the day. 8 of 10 lifts, 7 of 9 park features and 7 of 10 terrain zones are open. The Junior Nationals are running today in McPark and lower Lil Bucks, with a briefing from 8:30am; the Olympic Pipe and platter lift close at 12pm. The access road is chain-free, with an active road hazard advisory in place. The spring Pines Shuttle and bus schedule begins 1 October. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 8 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
